e\nEmergency Medicine\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nPrevious Slide\nNext Slide\nExpert Emergency and Specialty Care for Pets in Southeast Michigan\nMedVet Commerce is a premier animal emergency and specialty hospital serving Southeast Michigan. Our highly trained team serves as an extension of your family veterinarian’s care.\nServing more than 10,000 patients a year, our team is the trusted choice for family veterinarians and pet lovers. We know pets are an important part of your family, and we strive to provide exceptional care while showing you and your pet compassion. Our team has the expertise to skillfully deal with any pet emergency and provide advanced specialty care for your pet with the goal of getting your pet home to you in the best health.\nIf your pet is facing an emergency, you can come directly to our hospital – no appointment is needed.\nMedVet Commerce Caregivers\nSearch by Name\nFilter by Specialty\nAll Specialties\nCritical Care\nEmergency Medicine\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nSurgery\nOur Hospital Leaders\nJordan Assenmacher, DVM\nMedical Director\nAngie Heighton\nHospital Director\nOur Doctors\nJordan Assenmacher\n, DVM\nSydney Dudley\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nAdrienne Felix\n, DVM, DACVECC\nCritical Care, Emergency Medicine\nRachel Howard\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nMegan Lin\n, VMD, DACVIM (Neurology)\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nBrittany Losey\n, DVM, Limited to the Practice of Surgery\nSurgery\nLaura Miller\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nMelissa Morgan\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nAlex Politis\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nBernadette  Prettegiani\n, DVM, DACVS (Small Animal)\nSurgery\nEmily Starck\n, DVM\nEmergency Medicine\nPet Stories\n“\nOur almost 3 year old dog, Peaches, on leash was mauled by 2 much larger dogs MedVet rushed her in and attended to her with such lovely care. The vets and all of the staff were amazing. 1 month later and she is physically back to her old (young) self.\nPrevious Story\nNext Story\nFinancing Options\nWe understand that planning for the cost of care is important. Special financing and payment arrangements are available for qualified pet owners through an independent company, CareCredit.\nLearn More\nFind a location\nEmergency Care\nFind Care\nFind a Location\nFind A Doctor\nResources\nPet Care Resources\nClinical Studies\nAbout\nWe Are MedVet\nMedVet Experience\nOur Leaders\nOur Founders\nNewsroom\nDiversity, Inclusion, & Belonging\nCommunity Support\nFAQs\nContact Us\nFor Veterinarians\nClinical Studies\nContinuing Education\nCareers\nMedVet Open Positions at New Hospitals\nMedVet Training Programs\nSpecialties\nSpecialties Overview\nAnesthesia & Pain Management\nAvian & Exotics\nCardiology\nCritical Care\nDentistry & Oral Surgery\nDermatology\nEmergency Medicine\nIntegrative Medicine\nInternal Medicine\nInterventional Radiology\nMedical Oncology\nNeurology & Neurosurgery\nOphthalmology\nRadiation Oncology\nRadiology\nRehabilitation\nSports Medicine\nSurgery\nUrgent Care\nSocial\nInstagram\nLinkedIn\nFacebook\nYouTube\nPartners\nVetRad\nVeterinary Eye Institute\nMedVet Suppliers\nLegal\nPrivacy Policy\nCA Privacy\nYour Privacy Choices\nTerms\nTransparency in Coverage\nTax Information",
